From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:11:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: End a body cut short by the connection with a network
 error

A body that the connection ended early, before its Content-Length or its
last chunk, by an HTTP/2 stream reset with an error code, or by a TLS
connection closed inside a framed body, was handed over as complete and
the response marked aborted, like a body whose fetch was cancelled.
Consumers took the truncated body for the whole one: `fetch()` resolved
`text()` with it, XMLHttpRequest fired `load`, scripts ran it, style
sheets applied it, and a WebAssembly module cut at a section boundary
compiled.

When the stream errors in HTTP-network fetch, the fetch is a network
error, not aborted as a cancelled one is. End such a body with
`NetworkError::ConnectionFailure`, as one suspended for too long, and keep
ending a cancelled one, or one nobody can resume, as aborted. Devtools
gets a failed body as far as it got, as it does for an aborted one.

The previous patches prepare the consumers in script: `fetch()` errors
its body stream, EventSource reconnects, style sheets fail, XMLHttpRequest
drops what it received, and documents keep their fetch timing. Scripts,
workers and fonts already fail on a network error, and media restarts with
a range request. A truncated image is now broken instead of decoded as far
as the decoder accepts it, as in Chrome and WebKit.

Validation: `./mach test-unit -p servo-net`: 499 tests pass. New tests `test_body_cut_short_by_the_connection_is_a_network_error` (a short Content-Length and a chunk cut off, with the bytes received before the error handed over) and `test_body_cut_short_by_the_connection_is_sent_to_devtools`; `test_truncated_body_that_ends_with_its_tls_connection_is_a_network_error`, `test_fetch_whose_connection_closes_while_suspended_ends_when_resumed` and `test_truncated_response_is_not_served_from_cache` now expect `ConnectionFailure` instead of a delivered body, `test_body_cut_short_is_not_delivered_for_an_integrity_check` pins it, and the cancellation tests check that a cancelled body is not a network error. Against the previous patch, the six tests that expect `ConnectionFailure` or the devtools body fail. A focused WPT run (1132 tests: `fetch/api`, `fetch/content-*`, `fetch/http-cache`, `fetch/stale-while-revalidate`, `subresource-integrity`, `wasm/webapi`, `xhr`, `eventsource`, `navigation-timing`, the `link` and `style` element tests and the new tests) makes `fetch/api/basic/error-after-response.any.js` (6 subtests), `fetch/content-length/too-long.window.js`, `xhr/response-body-errors.any.js` (4) and `xhr/event-error.sub.any.js` (2) pass, as do the cut-short cases of the new tests; `fetch/stale-while-revalidate/stale-script.html` fails, as it does in 8 of 8 runs here on patch 115, because the revalidated response arrives after the test loads the script again.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent wrote this patch and its tests following docs/fetch-p4a-truncated-body-audit-2026-10-22.md in the workspace, and applied an independent review's findings)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
